# Backends are initialised per tier, never with --recursive: each carries its
# own nested submodules, and recursing pulls several gigabytes including three
# separate copies of Chipyard. Initialise only what the tier you want needs.
#
#   bench tier    git submodule update --init backends/zephyr-chipyard-sw
#   silicon tier  ... plus backends/chipyard   (Linux only; needs Vivado)
#   models        ... plus backends/modelblaster  (~143 MiB)
#   board files   git submodule update --init hardware/pcb   (KiCad, ~18 MiB)
#
# backends/modelblaster is the PyTorch -> quantized -> Zephyr/RISC-V compilation
# pipeline behind `rb modelblaster`. It is its own tier because it is an input to
# one flow rather than to the toolchain: every other workload builds without it,
# and it is the only backend whose codegen wants torch. It was a submodule of
# zephyr-chipyard-sw until nothing in that backend turned out to build against
# it; see docs/modelblaster-dronet-on-fpga.md.
#
# hardware/pcb is the board itself rather than a backend, and nothing in the
# build reads it, so no tier pulls it automatically. Initialise it when you
# need the schematic to answer a wiring question -- which net a sensor's XSHUT
# or interrupt pin actually reaches is the difference between a driver bug and
# an unwired pin, and this repo has been wrong about that before.
[submodule "backends/zephyr-chipyard-sw"]
	path = backends/zephyr-chipyard-sw
	url = https://github.com/lorenshung/zephyr-chipyard-sw.git
[submodule "backends/chipyard"]
	path = backends/chipyard
	url = https://github.com/lorenshung/chipyard.git
	branch = arty200t-dual-uart
[submodule "backends/modelblaster"]
	path = backends/modelblaster
	url = https://github.com/lorenshung/ModelBlaster.git
	# riskybird-integer-dronet, not main: this fork's merge of Dima's
	# ucb-bar/ModelBlaster branch of the same name -- integer DroNet kernels for
	# misa.F = 0, NHWC + conv0-pool fusion, the gemmini_q31_rvv backend -- with
	# the fork's Verilator runner, U250 target and per-config Gemmini headers.
	# main is 300+ commits behind and its int8 DroNet does not verify.
	branch = riskybird-integer-dronet
[submodule "hardware/pcb"]
	path = hardware/pcb
	url = https://github.com/lorenshung/riskybird.git
	branch = riskybirdv3-layout
